            <ArticleTitle>[Aortocoronary bypass in progressive stenocardia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors evaluate the efficacy of aortocoronary shunting in the treatment of 10 patients with progressive angina pectoris (unstable stenocardia) in follow-up periods of up to 12 months after the operation. In none of the patients did angina pectoris or myocardial infarction develop in the indicated postoperative periods.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
